Subject: [PATCH] #340 P3: redacting live-proof bundle builder (item 4) (#340)

* feat(evidence): redacting live-proof bundle builder + operator runner (#340)

Phase 3 item 4: turn a raw governed upcloud-ssh run into a committed,
secret-free bundle so LIVE VERIFIED claims are independently checkable.

- thinkbox/live_proof_bundle.py: re-hashes the artifact against the
  receipt, requires COMPLETED+verified, checks the provider, copies only
  an allow-listed field set, drops absolute paths and remote_user, and
  refuses private keys / bearer tokens / API keys / .ssh paths.
- scripts/run_live_proof_bundle.py: runs one exactly-allowed read-only
  command via UpCloudSSHExecutionAdapter, then builds the bundle.
- 17/17 hermetic tests; 40/40 with SSH adapter regression.

The bundle from a real worker-02 run is UNPROVEN: this worktree has the
historical dead host 212.147.250.183 and no SSH key (purged in #271).

* feat(infra): pin SSH host key + non-root support (Phase 3 item 3) (#340)

Fold item 3 into the #340 branch because it directly hardens the
provenance of the live-proof bundle item 4 produces.

- SSHWorkerConfig gains hardened + known_hosts_path; hardened argv uses
  StrictHostKeyChecking=yes + UserKnownHostsFile=<path> and never
  accept-new; validate() fails closed with a typed InvalidSSHConfig when
  hardened without a known_hosts source.
- UpCloudSSHExecutionConfig reads UPCLOUD_SSH_HARDENED and
  UPCLOUD_SSH_KNOWN_HOSTS; is_complete() returns False when hardened
  without known_hosts; is_non_root() makes the non-root expectation
  explicit; username stays parameterized. root is documented as a dev
  default, not the recommended production configuration.
- .env.example documents the five UpCloud SSH vars; runner surfaces
  hardened mode in its diagnostic.
- Focused tests + mutation proof (removing the pinning branch fails 2
  tests); targeted regression set 103/103 OK.

Not LIVE VERIFIED: no real worker-02 run. Dead host 212.147.250.183 and
the purged key ~/.ssh/kilo-upcloud were not touched.

